  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1203 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nSurface high pressure will pass by to the north today into \nFriday providing much drier and cooler conditions. High \ntemperatures today will only rise into the low to mid 80s, and \nupper 70s to low 80s on Thursday and Friday. Lows will drop into\nthe 60s. A shortwave moving out of the plains will bring rain \nchances (30-50%) back into the region on Friday into Saturday \nmorning. PWs climb back above 2\" so heavy rain may be something\nto keep an eye on. Behind the shortwave, upper level ridging \nexpands across the plains with the region on the eastern \nperiphery of the ridge. Temperatures will rise back into the 90s\nalong with an increase in humidity.",
